Wed Oct 19 17:42:27 1994  John Salmon  (johns@mullet.anu.edu.au)

	* libsw/Msgs.c, error.c: try to prevent and/or minimize the damage
	caused by recursion.  Now that the Msgs may be delivered by MPMY
	functions, and those MPMY functions themselves might generate Msgs,
	this is critical.

	* libmpmy/mpmy_*io.[ch] (MPMY_Fopen): Added a new 'mode':  
	MPMY_INDEPENDENT.  There was some ambiguity about the MPMY_UNIX
	mode, which is now resolved as follows:  UNIX opens the same file
	name, and perhaps conserves some precious resources (e.g., fd's).
	INDEPENDENT opens totally and completely independent files.
	MPMY_Fiomode now has some hard-to-define restrictions.  Better
	to not use it at all and just close the file...

	* libsw/msgdirinit.c (MsgdirInit): Don't use stdio.h.  Use
	mpmy_io.h, MPMY_Vfprintf and MPMY_Flush instead.  Is this the
	last of the stdio.h-isms?

	* libmpmy/io_generic.c: Added functions MPMY_Fprintf, Vfprintf
	and Fflush.  Added them, along with Fiomode to the .h file.
	Implementations are in io_generic.c, #include'd in mpmy_*io.c.

