Thu Sep  8 09:44:11 1994  Mike Warren  (msw@sampson)

	* relerr/main_nv.c (main): Don't read or save nterms.  With
	the frac mac, the first step would be imbalanced anyway.
	(main): Clear acc, phi and nterms here, rather than in InheritSink.
	This is necessary to accumulate values during multiple calls to
	walk for the periodic bc code.

	* libtree/walk.c (WalkInit,WalkNT,WalkTerminate) Same as Walk, but 
	doesn't terminate the polling machinery until WalkTerminate.  By
	eliminating the synchronization one can do a series of imbalanced
	traversals (for instance to do periodic boundary conditions)
	without the load imbalance penalty.

	* relerr/grav_nv.c (SetGravOffset): Shift the sinks by the
	amount specified.
	
	* relerr/main_nv.c (Periodic): Enable use of periodic BC.

	* libsw/randoms.c (cube_rand): For generating cubes to test the
	periodic boundary code.

