	synchronous mode Bcast if iomode is MPMY_SINGL.

	* libmpmy/mpmy_{unixio,paragonio,cm5io}.c (MPMY_Fopen): Make 
	return value 0 if open returns -1.  We were confusing all of the
	code that assumes fopen returns NULL on failure.

	* libSDF/SDFfuncs.c: Add an MPMY_IOZERO flag to the open in SDFissdf.

Fri Sep  2 09:35:33 1994  Mike Warren  (msw@sampson)

	* libsw/Malloc.c: Warn if large malloc is attempted.  This might
	help explain abnormal behavior on a virtual memory machine like
	the paragon.

	* relerr/main_nv.c (HeapCnt) SunOS evidently has a symbol in
	the name space called HeapCnt, so we name it HeapCnt_.

	* libmpmy/mpmy_generic.c: decrease MAXCOMM to 250, and sleep
	for a second if it looks like space is short.

	* libmpmy/mpmy_nx.c: Use _isend and _irecv[x] instead of 
	plain versions.

	* libsw/malloc.c (malloc_used): New function which tells how
	much heap space has been obtained from the OS.

	* libsw/do_sigs.c: Add a PrintMemfile() to sw_handler().

